WEBVTT

00:10:29.800 --> 00:10:33.816
She says, "You have to be all things.

00:10:33.840 --> 00:10:35.456
Why exclude?

00:10:35.480 --> 00:10:38.040
You have to be everything."

00:10:39.240 --> 00:10:41.616
And Tharp's method

00:10:41.640 --> 00:10:45.976
for preventing all of these different
projects from becoming overwhelming

00:10:46.000 --> 00:10:47.296
is a simple one.

00:10:47.320 --> 00:10:49.856
She gives each project
a big cardboard box,

00:10:49.880 --> 00:10:52.576
writes the name of the project
on the side of the box.

00:10:52.600 --> 00:10:57.016
And into it, she tosses DVDs
and books, magazine cuttings,

00:10:57.040 --> 00:10:59.016
theater programs, physical objects,

00:10:59.040 --> 00:11:04.016
really anything that's provided a source
of creative inspiration.